surname>Grimshaw</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What do we know about how to do audit and feedback? Pitfalls in applying evidence from a systematic review</article-title><source>BMC Health Serv Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>50</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16011811</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eccles</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Grimshaw</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnston</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pitts</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changing the behaviour of healthcare professionals: the use of theory in promoting the uptake of research findings</article-title><source>J Clin Epidemiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>112</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15680740</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oxman</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Fretheim</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Flottorp</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The OFF theory of research utilization</article-title><source>J Clin Epidemiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>116</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15680741</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>The Improved Clinical Effectiveness through Behavioural Research</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Designing theoretically-informed implementa